   128	exactly as untrustworthy as the offset, so the rebuild runs and out-of-band
   129	rows are lost with it. Checking counts *before* rebuilding would block
   130	legitimate recoveries; two abnormal events have to stack to reach that
   131	window.
   132	
   133	The counts are never cached per handle: every stamp derives them from the
   134	*committed* marker, read under the write lock the INSERT already took. Two
