   130	def _canonical_bytes(obj: object) -> bytes:
   131	    """Canonical encoding for commitment hashing: JCS, RFC 8785.
   132	
   133	    Upgraded from implementation-local json.dumps 2026-06-12
   134	    (decision design/attestation-canonicalization-jcs): the Go conformance
   135	    oracle is the federation-facing consumer the original docstring named
   136	    as the upgrade trigger, and cross-implementation hash divergence
   137	    renders as a false tamper alarm. Pre-JCS chains were re-anchored at
   138	    the swap (sl store reanchor), not grandfathered — SPEC §8.1.
   139	
   140	    Stored payload TEXT is still embedded verbatim as a string value, so
   141	    hashes detect byte-level tampering without re-serialization concerns
   142	    leaking in from payload content.
   143	    """
   144	    return rfc8785.dumps(obj)
