   551	    def _ceremony_persist(self, rows: list[tuple]) -> None:
   552	        """Make a declaration ceremony canonical: one durable line, stamped.
   553	
   554	        Runs inside the ceremony's open ``BEGIN IMMEDIATE`` transaction,
   555	        after every CAS check passed and the fact INSERTs (+ meta stamps)
   556	        are staged, immediately before the caller's COMMIT — the same shape
   557	        as :meth:`_write` steps 3–4. One row serializes as a plain fact
   558	        line; several as one ``batch`` envelope line (the log's atomicity
   559	        unit), so recovery can never expose a partial ceremony. Any failure
   560	        after the fsync rolls the index back and leaves the line durable
   561	        and unindexed — the standard recoverable state the next
   562	        open/reconcile tails forward, all N rows atomically.
